    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for `POST /api/owners`, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `customerCode` field mapped to a `customer_code` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schemas** \u2014 added `customer_code` to the `owners` table in all four DDL files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres); tests run on hsqldb.\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it (and MapStruct maps it automatically on the way out).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 ignored `customerCode` on `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (consistent with `id`/`pets`), since the code is assigned by the pipeline, not the request body.\n\n5. **New function** `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` \u2014 a single-responsibility step that mutates the built `Owner` in place: `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of the last name (clamped for short names), `NNNN` = `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits.\n\n6. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignCustomerCode` into the pipeline after `defaultRegistrationDate` and before `save`, under the same `transaction` governance so the count and insert are consistent.\n\nThis follows the project's OfficeFloor conventions (one function class = one step = one responsibility) and reuses the existing `Default\u2026`-style mutate-in-place pattern rather than bloating `BuildOwner` or `SaveOwner`. The acceptance test and full suite pass.",
